# CONTAINMENT, not size (Critical Rule 1 + credential hygiene): the example's
# Docker build context is the REPO ROOT, and .gitignore does NOT gate a Docker
# build. This working tree holds `.env` (secrets) and `erl_crash.dump` (an
# Erlang heap dump that can contain decoded row values) — a size-motivated
# ignore list would let them ride the context into image layers.
#
# Whitelist form: deny EVERYTHING, re-allow only the paths the example's
# Dockerfile COPYs. A future untracked file (a crash dump, a .env.local, a
# lifecycle artifact) is excluded by construction.

*

!mix.exs
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!lib
!lib/**
!examples/replication_pipeline/mix.exs
!examples/replication_pipeline/mix.lock
!examples/replication_pipeline/config
!examples/replication_pipeline/config/**
!examples/replication_pipeline/lib
!examples/replication_pipeline/lib/**
